/* Guanyin oracle data (English) · sources noted in docs/qian-data-sources/guanyin.md */
window.QIAN_DATA = {
  id: "guanyin",
  total: 100,
  name: "Guanyin Oracle Sticks",
  nameZh: "观音灵签",
  grades: ["上签", "中签", "下签"],
  gradeLabels: { "上签": "Favorable", "中签": "Neutral", "下签": "Lower" },
  aspects: ["Marriage", "Career", "Wealth", "Health"],
  signs: [
    { no: 1, grade: "上签", titleZh: "钟离成道", title: "Zhongli Quan Attains the Dao", poemZh: "开天辟地作良缘\n吉日良时万物全\n若得此签非小可\n人行忠正帝王宣", poem: "Heaven and earth divide — a destined bond begins;\nOn an auspicious day, all things are whole.\nTo draw this sign is no small matter:\nWalk upright and loyal, and the throne will call for you.", meaning: "Zhongli Quan persevered through long cultivation to reach immortality. Like the first parting of heaven and earth, this sign opens a favorable new chapter: conditions are ripe, the timing is right, and noble helpers will value your integrity. Advance boldly in your career; marriage promises happiness, wealth flows smoothly, and health holds steady. As the first of the hundred signs, it is bright throughout — move forward with confidence.", aspects: ["Heaven-made match", "Noble support", "Flows smoothly", "Sound health"] },
    { no: 2, grade: "下签", titleZh: "苏秦不第", title: "Su Qin Fails the Exams", poemZh: "鲸鱼未变守江河\n不可升腾更望高\n异日峥嵘身变化\n许君一跃跳龙门", poem: "The whale, not yet transformed, keeps to the river;\nIt cannot soar aloft, nor crave the heights.\nOne day, majestic, its form will change —\nThen you may leap the Dragon Gate in a single bound.", meaning: "Su Qin knew repeated failure before his rise. Like a whale still lurking in the river, your time has not yet come, and forcing your way upward will only bring setbacks. Endure and be patient; build your strength while you wait. Marriage is hard to settle now, money comes grudgingly, and health needs care. If you can hold steady through this low point, leaping the Dragon Gate still lies ahead.", aspects: ["Hard to settle", "Wait and build", "Lean returns", "Care needed"] },
    { no: 3, grade: "下签", titleZh: "董永卖身", title: "Dong Yong Sells Himself", poemZh: "临风冒雨去还乡\n正是其身似燕儿\n衔得泥来欲作垒\n到头垒坏复须泥", poem: "Braving wind and rain you journey home again,\nYour very self like a swallow in the storm;\nIt carries mud to build its nest,\nYet the nest crumbles — mud is needed once more.", meaning: "Dong Yong sold himself into servitude to bury his father — devotion rewarded only after hardship. Like a swallow whose rebuilt nest keeps collapsing, your efforts now yield less than they cost; relationships drift and plans unravel if you cling too tightly. Yet the pattern here turns from bad to good. Keep to your duties without greed or haste, expect modest returns, and watch your strength. Stepping back brings stability.", aspects: ["Unsettled ties", "Toil, little gain", "Modest returns", "Guard strain"] },
    { no: 4, grade: "上签", titleZh: "玉莲会十朋", title: "Yulian Meets Shipeng", poemZh: "千年古镜复重圆\n女再求夫男再婚\n自此门庭重改换\n更添福禄在儿孙", poem: "The ancient mirror, long broken, is made whole again;\nA woman may seek a husband anew, a man may wed again.\nFrom this day the household changes its face,\nAnd fortune and blessing multiply in children and grandchildren.", meaning: "Wang Shipeng and Qian Yulian, torn apart by intrigue, finally reunited — a broken mirror joined anew. Whatever was lost returns in better form: old ties resume, a marriage concludes after trials, the whole household enters a brighter era. Your toil brings real gains, especially from autumn onward. Cherish those around you and treat them sincerely — reunion is the heart of this sign.", aspects: ["Reunion", "Effort rewarded", "Rising, autumn luck", "Pray for peace"] },
    { no: 5, grade: "中签", titleZh: "刘晨遇仙", title: "Liu Chen Meets Immortals", poemZh: "一锥草地要求泉\n努力求之得最难\n无意俄然遇知己\n相逢携手上青天", poem: "With a single awl you dig the grassland, seeking a spring;\nStrive as you may, it is the hardest thing to win.\nThen, all unlooked-for, you meet a kindred spirit,\nAnd hand in hand you rise into the blue.", meaning: "Liu Chen went into the Tiantai mountains to gather herbs and met immortals — fortune arriving unannounced. Digging for a spring with an awl, effort alone moves slowly; better to stand firm where you are and let the moment ripen. When the pursuit grows wearying, a true friend or backer appears, and together you rise. Marriage can come together, money stays level. Do not rush — wait for the helper.", aspects: ["Can unite", "Hold and plan", "Steady, no rush", "Untroubled"] },
    { no: 6, grade: "中签", titleZh: "仁贵遇主", title: "Rengui Meets His Lord", poemZh: "投身岩下雕鸟居\n须是还他大丈夫\n及早营谋谁可得\n通行天地此人无", poem: "He casts himself beneath the cliff where the eagle dwells;\nSuch a man must still be honored as a hero.\nWho could win through by eager scheming?\nNone other can range the earth and sky as he.", meaning: "Xue Rengui, a poor farmer, joined the army and was at last discovered by his lord. This sign shows a capable person overlooked in a low position — poor, patient, but impossible to overshadow. Present circumstances are plain, so do not complain; keep your integrity and sharpen your skills. When the patron who recognizes you appears, your rise will be swift. Marriage stays modest; money trends slowly upward.", aspects: ["Steady, slow", "Await a patron", "Slowly improves", "Calm mind"] },
    { no: 7, grade: "下签", titleZh: "苏娘走难", title: "Su Niang Flees Calamity", poemZh: "奔波阻隔重重险\n带水拖坭去度山\n更望他乡求用事\n千乡万里未回还", poem: "Toiling onward, blocked by danger upon danger,\nThrough mud and water you drag across the hills;\nSeek your fortunes in another land, and —\nA thousand towns, ten thousand miles, no returning.", meaning: "Su Niang fled through hardship after hardship. This sign says retreat is possible but advance is perilous: long journeys, relocations, and reaches for the heights all bring obstacles, and what you pursue in far places may never come home. Marriage needs blessing to smooth; dealings stay flat; see to ailments early. Hold your ground, keep the old and familiar, and let the storm pass — safety lies in standing still.", aspects: ["Needs blessing", "Stay put", "Luck after autumn", "Tend early"] },
    { no: 8, grade: "上签", titleZh: "斐度还带", title: "Pei Du Returns the Belt", poemZh: "茂林松柏正兴旺\n雨雪风霜总莫为\n异日忽然成大用\n功名成就栋梁材", poem: "Pine and cypress flourish in the lush grove;\nRain, snow, wind and frost can do them no harm.\nOne day, suddenly, they serve the greatest use —\nHonor won, a timber for pillar and beam.", meaning: "Pei Du returned a precious belt he found, and that hidden virtue later raised him to chancellor. Like sturdy pines in a dense grove, your foundations are deep; hardship cannot wear them down. For those who keep doing good, the road runs open: a career with real responsibility, family fortunes growing day by day, and earnings steady though not spectacular. Stay upright, and the rewards keep arriving.", aspects: ["Fine match", "Great usefulness", "Steady rise", "Safe and well"] },
    { no: 9, grade: "中签", titleZh: "孔明点将", title: "Kongming Musters His Generals", poemZh: "烦君勿作私心事\n此意偏宜说问公\n一片明心光皎洁\n宛如皎月正天中", poem: "Pray do not harbor secret, private schemes;\nYour thoughts are best declared for the common good.\nA clear heart shines pure and spotless,\nLike the bright moon at the very center of the sky.", meaning: "Zhuge Kongming dispatched his generals with rewards and penalties laid bare. The full moon images a clean heart: act from fairness, not private calculation, and a clear answer will follow. Taking the honest road in your work earns trust; marriage can conclude, money stays middling, and health is calm. Before any move, examine your motives — where there is no guilt, there is no harm.", aspects: ["Sincerity wins", "Honest road", "Fair, middling", "Calm and well"] },
    { no: 10, grade: "中签", titleZh: "庞涓观阵", title: "Pang Juan Surveys the Formation", poemZh: "石藏无价玉和珍\n只管他乡外客寻\n宛如持灯更觅火\n不如收拾枉劳心", poem: "A priceless jade lies hidden in the stone,\nYet you search for it only in other lands;\nIt is like carrying a lamp to look for fire —\nBetter to gather it in, this wasted toil of heart.", meaning: "Pang Juan studied the enemy formation and lost sight of the whole. This sign shows someone holding a lamp while hunting for fire: treasure already lies in your own stone — why ask strangers elsewhere? The difficulty you face is a matter of direction, not effort. Money and deals stall; only a relationship can come together. Stop reaching outward, take stock of what you carry, and save your strength.", aspects: ["Can unite", "Look within", "Stop in time", "Rest quietly"] },
    { no: 11, grade: "上签", titleZh: "书荐姜维", title: "A Letter Recommends Jiang Wei", poemZh: "欲求胜事可非常\n争奈亲姻日暂忙\n到头竟必成中箭\n贵人指引贵人乡", poem: "To seek a surpassing deed is no common task,\nAnd kin and obligations keep you briefly busy;\nYet in the end the mark is surely struck —\nA noble guide leads on to a noble land.", meaning: "One letter of recommendation made Jiang Wei's career. This sign points to a patron's introduction. The goal you pursue is extraordinary; though days are crowded and ties demand attention, the matter concludes safely in the end. Draw near to upright, helpful people and ask for their guidance — with an endorsement, the road turns splendid. Household luck is high, marriage agrees, and money comes in. Seize the connection.", aspects: ["United success", "Guided upward", "Gains in reach", "Smooth and safe"] },
    { no: 12, grade: "上签", titleZh: "武吉遇师", title: "Wu Ji Meets His Master", poemZh: "否去泰来咫尺间\n暂交君子出于山\n若逢虎兔佳音信\n立志忙中事即闲", poem: "Ill fortune goes, good fortune comes — a foot's distance only;\nFor a time you walk with gentlemen, down out of the hills.\nMeet Tiger or Rabbit, and good news will arrive;\nWith resolve, the busiest task turns easy.", meaning: "Wu Ji, guilty of a death, was guided by Jiang Ziya and escaped disaster — blessing born of misfortune. The turn from bad to good is closer than it looks; the narrow stretch with worthy companions is nearly over. In Tiger or Rabbit months, expect glad tidings; set your purpose firmly and busyness eases into calm. Marriage can be concluded, money will come, and health improves after autumn. Hold on.", aspects: ["Happy match", "Luck from loss", "Gains to come", "Better in autumn"] },
    { no: 13, grade: "中签", titleZh: "罗通拜帅", title: "Luo Tong Takes Command", poemZh: "自小生在富贵家\n眼前万物总奢华\n蒙君赐紫金腰带\n四海声名定可夸", poem: "Born and raised in a wealthy, honored house,\nEverything before your eyes is splendor;\nThe sovereign grants a belt of purple gold,\nAnd your name is praised across the four seas.", meaning: "Luo Tong was made marshal while still a youth — glory that still calls for prudence. Born to comfort and surrounded by luxury, with a reputation to carry far, you yet need gratitude and restraint to make it last. As a prisoner gains pardon and the sick grow well, current constraints will loosen and distinction follows. Marriage agrees; act after autumn for better luck — nothing needs forcing now.", aspects: ["Can unite", "Fame in time", "Autumn improves", "Eases, recovers"] },
    { no: 14, grade: "中签", titleZh: "子牙弃官", title: "Ziya Resigns His Office", poemZh: "宛如仙鹤出凡笼\n脱得凡笼路路通\n南北东西无阻隔\n任君直上九霄宫", poem: "Like an immortal crane escaping the mortal cage,\nFreed from the cage, every road runs clear;\nNorth, south, east, west — nothing bars the way:\nRise straight up to the palace of the ninth heaven.", meaning: "Jiang Ziya resigned a petty post and later met King Wen, changing history. This sign is the crane leaving its cage: once confinement releases, every direction opens, and nothing obstructs the climb. If you are stuck in a stifling place, step away resolutely and make a fresh field. Marriage agrees, money has its roads, and travel or a move goes well. Release the attachment — the sky is wide.", aspects: ["Free agreement", "Breakthrough", "Roads open", "Body at ease"] },
    { no: 15, grade: "中签", titleZh: "苏秦得志", title: "Su Qin Attains His Ambition", poemZh: "行人怨日气难吞\n忽有灾事勿近前\n鸟破林巢无所宿\n可寻深处稳安身", poem: "The traveler curses the sun, his anger hard to swallow;\nWhen sudden trouble stirs, draw not near.\nThe bird's forest nest is broken, nowhere to lodge —\nSeek out the deep recesses to rest secure.", meaning: "Su Qin studied through humiliation and at last wore the seals of six states. For now, like a bird whose nest is shattered or a traveler swallowing anger, the moment stings; find safe, quiet ground and let the noise pass. Gossip need not be answered; kind words are not all true. The pattern runs from rough to smooth: money arrives, romance briefly stalls. Outlast this stretch — vindication follows.", aspects: ["Briefly stalled", "Sweet after bitter", "Eventually gains", "Vow, find calm"] },
    { no: 16, grade: "中签", titleZh: "叶梦熊朝帝", title: "Ye Mengxiong Before the Emperor", poemZh: "愁眉思虑暂时开\n启出云霄喜自来\n宛如粪土中藏玉\n良工荐举出尘埃", poem: "The worried brow unknits, dark thoughts lift;\nAbove the clouds, joy comes of its own accord.\nLike fine jade hidden in common earth,\nA master's hand raises it out of the dust.", meaning: "Ye Mengxiong stood before the emperor and was found worthy — true jade recognized in the dirt. Your knotted brow is about to smooth: talent concealed until now awaits the discerning expert whose recommendation draws it into the light. Small-minded people meet trouble; the principled ride the change well. Marriage and money both conclude, but advance gradually rather than rushing. The turning point arrives with your benefactor.", aspects: ["Good match", "Master's praise", "Gradual gains", "Blessed peace"] },
    { no: 17, grade: "中签", titleZh: "话梅止渴", title: "Plums to Quench Thirst", poemZh: "莫听闲言说是非\n晨昏只好念阿弥\n若将狂话为真实\n书饼如何止得饥", poem: "Do not heed idle gossip and disputes;\nMorning and evening, better to recite the Buddha's name.\nTake wild words for truth, and —\nHow can a painted cake still your hunger?", meaning: "Gazing at plums never quenches thirst, nor a painted cake hunger: imagination cannot replace substance. This sign warns the unsettled heart against taking fine words as facts. Empty promises in love deserve no trust; glittering profits that cannot be cashed deserve no chase. Ground yourself in what is real, for that alone dissolves the thirst. Matters look smooth but hide friction — hold, do not push.", aspects: ["Distrust promises", "Be practical", "Move slowly", "Peace of mind"] },
    { no: 18, grade: "上签", titleZh: "曹国舅为仙", title: "Cao Guojiu Becomes an Immortal", poemZh: "金乌西坠兔东升\n日夜循环至古今\n僧道得知无不利\n士农工商各从心", poem: "The golden crow sinks west, the hare rises east;\nDay into night, the cycle runs from old to now.\nMonks and Daoists gain without fail;\nScholar, farmer, artisan, merchant — each follows his heart.", meaning: "Cao Guojiu traded wealth and rank for immortality — the sign of a natural, unhindered cycle. As the sun sets the moon rises: fortunes turn in your favor, the heart carries no burden, and whatever is undertaken succeeds like an arrow loosed at mid-flight. People of every calling prosper by following their own nature. Marriage agrees, income flows, health shines. Act freely — the season is yours.", aspects: ["Perfect union", "Each thrives", "Smooth income", "Blessed health"] },
    { no: 19, grade: "中签", titleZh: "子仪封王", title: "Ziyi Enfeoffed as Prince", poemZh: "急水滩头放船归\n风波作波欲何为\n若要安然求稳静\n等待浪静过此危", poem: "At the rapids' head you launch the boat for home;\nThe wind kicks waves — what can be done?\nIf you would pass in safety and in calm,\nThen wait until the water stills before crossing.", meaning: "Guo Ziyi won a princehood, yet even he knew to respect the rapids. This sign is a boat released at fast shallows: waves are rising, and forcing through invites capsizing. Your plans, money, and even a match are simply not ripe — the issue is timing, not worth. Keep to the old routine, gather merit quietly, and let the wind turn. Never row hard at the crest of the wave.", aspects: ["Not yet time", "Wait for calm", "Not yet", "Pray for safety"] },
    { no: 20, grade: "中签", titleZh: "姜太公遇文王", title: "Jiang Taigong Meets King Wen", poemZh: "当春久雨喜开晴\n玉兔金乌渐渐明\n旧事消散新事遂\n看看一跳遇龙门", poem: "After long spring rains, the sky clears in joy;\nHare and crow grow brighter by degrees.\nOld matters scatter, new matters succeed —\nWatch now: one leap, and the Dragon Gate is met.", meaning: "Jiang Taigong fished at the Wei River past seventy before King Wen found him — great talent, late blooming. The long rain is ending; sun and moon brighten by turns, old entanglements dissolve, and fresh ventures take shape until, suddenly, you leap the Dragon Gate. Fortune is turning but not yet turned: keep doing good, hold your hook patiently, and the moment will meet you. Patience is your best strategy.", aspects: ["Comes at will", "Late but certain", "Arrives in time", "Safe through storms"] },
    { no: 21, grade: "上签", titleZh: "李旦龙凤配合", title: "Li Dan's Dragon-Phoenix Match", poemZh: "阴阳道合总由天\n女嫁男婚喜偎然\n但见龙蛇相会合\n熊罴入梦乐团圆", poem: "The way of yin and yang joins by Heaven's decree;\nA woman weds, a man takes a bride — joy upon joy.\nWhen dragon and serpent meet in harmony,\nBears enter the dream: a house made glad and whole.", meaning: "Li Dan and Hu Fengjiao were matched like dragon and phoenix — a union arranged by heaven itself. This sign radiates harmony: marriage is blessed, a son may be announced, and family and estate flourish together. Plans proceed as the heart wishes, with patrons lending a hand at every step. Flow with the current of good feeling rather than forcing outcomes — completeness arrives on its own.", aspects: ["Heaven-sent match", "Wishes fulfilled", "Fortune grows", "Good remedy"] },
    { no: 22, grade: "中签", titleZh: "六郎逢救", title: "Six Lang Finds Rescue", poemZh: "旱时田里皆枯槁\n谢天甘雨落淋淋\n花果草木皆润泽\n始知一雨值千金", poem: "In drought the fields all withered dry;\nThen — thanks be to Heaven — sweet rain pours down.\nFlowers, fruit, grass and trees drink their fill,\nAnd you learn what one rain is worth in gold.", meaning: "Yang Six Lang, surrounded and starving, was rescued in time — this sign is rain after long drought. A withered situation is about to be watered: what looked dead greens again, and you discover how much one timely rescue is worth. Fortune creeps back, illness meets its remedy, money shows real profit. Travelers and news may lag a little. Be grateful for the helpers, and let the field renew itself.", aspects: ["Revived", "Turning point", "Real returns", "Right remedy"] },
    { no: 23, grade: "中签", titleZh: "怀德招亲", title: "Huaide Wins a Bride", poemZh: "欲扳仙桂入蟾宫\n普开天门不任君\n忽遇一般音信好\n人人皆笑岭顶花", poem: "You would pluck the magic cassia in the Toad Palace;\nThe gates of Heaven open wide — yet not for you.\nThen suddenly good word arrives,\nWhile everyone laughs at the flower on the peak.", meaning: "Gao Huaide won his bride; ambition aimed at the cassia in the moon palace. Heaven's gate stands open, yet your name is not on the list: the wish waits one step away. Don't lose heart; unexpected news will signal the turn. Laughter at the peak's lone flower only proves how high you aim. Money and trade go well; watch your steps. Climb steadily — the plucking day will come.", aspects: ["Blocked, await word", "Climb steadily", "Profits flow", "Well and safe"] },
    { no: 24, grade: "下签", titleZh: "殷郊遇师", title: "Yin Jiao Meets His Master", poemZh: "不成理论不成家\n水性痴人似落花\n若问君恩须得力\n到头方见事如麻", poem: "No settled doctrine, no established house;\nThe shallow-hearted drift like falling petals.\nAsk whether favor's strength will hold —\nAt the end, matters tangle like hemp.", meaning: "Yin Jiao defied his master's command and met ruin — a warning about unstable foundations. Without settled principles, neither household nor career holds together, and a mind like petals on water drifts wherever the current pulls. Counting on favor and forcing outcomes only tangles matters worse. Speak little of disputes, guard your gates, and keep your conscience straight — that is the way through. Romance waits; money is blocked.", aspects: ["Wait for stability", "Mind your words", "Blocked, persist", "Seek protection"] },
    { no: 25, grade: "中签", titleZh: "李广机智", title: "Li Guang's Resourcefulness", poemZh: "过了忧危事几重\n从今再立永无空\n宽心自有宽心计\n得遇高人立大功", poem: "The layers of danger and care are past;\nFrom now, what you build will never come to nothing.\nAn easy heart will find its easy plan;\nMeet a wise one, and great deeds are won.", meaning: "Li Guang's quick wit carried him through ambush after ambush. The perilous chapters are behind you; whatever you establish now rests on solid ground and will not collapse. Though things move slowly, do not fret — a calm mind writes its own plan, and a capable adviser turns it into real achievement. A match finds harmony; a dispute finds justice. Compose yourself, lay the groundwork, and success follows.", aspects: ["Harmony found", "Rebuild solidly", "Slowly unblocks", "Safe and sound"] },
    { no: 26, grade: "中签", titleZh: "钟馗得道", title: "Zhong Kui Attains the Dao", poemZh: "上下传来事转虚\n天边接得一封书\n书中许我功名遂\n直到终时亦是虚", poem: "Word comes down from above — and turns to mist;\nFrom the sky's edge a letter falls into your hands.\nIt promises you rank and fame fulfilled,\nYet to the very end, empty it remains.", meaning: "Zhong Kui failed the examinations yet became a demon-quelling deity — worldly loss, transcendent gain. The letter you receive promises glittering success, but read it twice: news passed up and down is mostly vapor, and the higher the hope, the harder the fall. Longing for fame is worth less than a settled, safe present. Check every bright promise against the ledger, keep to your honest routine — the true attainment.", aspects: ["Hard to trust", "Keep the old", "Distrust promises", "Pray for health"] },
    { no: 27, grade: "中签", titleZh: "刘基谏主", title: "Liu Ji Counsels His Lord", poemZh: "一谋一用一番书\n虑后思前不敢为\n时到贵人相助力\n如山墙立可安居", poem: "One plan, one move, one memorial written;\nWeighing after and before, you dare not act.\nBut when the hour comes, a patron lends strength,\nAnd like a mountain wall you stand, and dwell at ease.", meaning: "Liu Ji advised the founding emperor with careful, patient memorials. This sign is the old made new — a winter flower meeting spring: former blockages dissolve and plans begin to satisfy. Your current hesitation, weighing every step, is wisdom rather than weakness. When the moment arrives, helpers appear unbidden and, like a wall of mountain stone, you may settle in security. Romance opens after delay; money comes at last.", aspects: ["Opens after delay", "Advise, then act", "Comes at last", "Slowly mends"] },
    { no: 28, grade: "中签", titleZh: "李后寻包公", title: "Empress Li Seeks Judge Bao", poemZh: "东边月上正婵娟\n顷刻云遮亦暗存\n或有圆时还有缺\n更言非者亦闲言", poem: "In the east the moon rides full and lovely;\nIn an instant clouds veil it — light hidden, not lost.\nThere are hours of fullness and hours of lack;\nLet the fault-finders talk: theirs is idle breath.", meaning: "Empress Li's grievance was at last cleared by Judge Bao — truth keeps its own calendar. Like a full moon suddenly veiled, your light is dimmed but not extinguished; clouds pass, and fullness and waning each have their season. Do not wear yourself out on doubters' chatter. Keep your footing and your inner clarity, and wait: when the clouds scatter, the record is set right before everyone's eyes.", aspects: ["Clears at last", "Hold steady", "Hidden, not lost", "Slowly heals"] },
    { no: 29, grade: "中签", titleZh: "赵子龙救阿斗", title: "Zhao Zilong Rescues Adou", poemZh: "宝剑出匣耀光明\n在匣全然不惹尘\n今得贵人携出现\n有威有势众人钦", poem: "The precious sword leaves its case, blazing light;\nWhile cased, it gathered never a speck of dust.\nNow a patron carries it forth to show the world —\nWith power and presence, all the crowd bows.", meaning: "Zhao Zilong carried the infant lord through a sea of spears — the sword finally out of its case. Your talent, long sheathed and spotless, is being drawn into the open by a backer who knows its worth; authority and admiration follow. This is the moment to volunteer for the hard assignment. Marriage goes well, money turns a profit. Remember who lifted you, and let the bright blade stay humble.", aspects: ["Well matched", "Blaze forth", "Profit likely", "Vow, stay well"] },
    { no: 30, grade: "中签", titleZh: "棋盘大会", title: "The Chessboard Assembly", poemZh: "劝君切莫向他求\n似鹤飞来暗箭投\n若去采薪蛇在草\n恐遭毒口也忧愁", poem: "I counsel you: do not go asking elsewhere;\nA crane flies in — and hidden arrows fly with it.\nGo to gather brushwood, and snakes lie in the grass;\nMeet their venom, and sorrow follows close.", meaning: "The Chessboard Assembly concealed ambush within ceremony — danger crouching behind courtesy. A lone crane draws arrows; the grass hides snakes. This is a sign to shut the mouth, mind your own affairs, and refuse anything touched by bad faith, lest the harm circle home. Money waits for its season, romance is withheld, and a stubborn ailment asks for patient treatment. Keep your head low, away from where snakes feed.", aspects: ["Not granted", "Duck the arrows", "Wait for season", "Patient care"] },
    { no: 31, grade: "中签", titleZh: "佛印会东坡", title: "Foyin Meets Dongpo", poemZh: "清闲无忧静处坐\n饱后吃茶时坐卧\n放下身心不用忙\n必定不招冤与祸", poem: "At ease and untroubled, sitting in a quiet place;\nAfter a full meal, tea, and resting at will;\nLay body and mind down — no need to hurry —\nAnd surely no wrong or harm will find you.", meaning: "The monk Foyin and Su Dongpo traded verses in leisure. This sign is quiet sitting after the meal: nothing outside demands rescue, so stop stirring. Anxiety itself invents the trouble it fears; a settled heart invites no lawsuits or misfortune. Keep duties simple, sip the tea, and let matters mature on their own — health especially thanks you for slowing down.", aspects: ["Unhurried bond", "Stay steady", "Enough as is", "Well kept"] },
    { no: 32, grade: "中签", titleZh: "刘备求贤", title: "Liu Bei Seeks Worthies", poemZh: "前程杳杳定无疑\n石中藏玉有谁知\n一朝良匠分明剖\n始觉安然碧玉期", poem: "The road ahead is dim, yet settled beyond doubt;\nWho knows the jade hidden in the stone?\nOne day a master hand cuts it clean apart —\nThen you feel at ease: the season of green jade.", meaning: "Liu Bei crossed rivers and snow to recruit sleeping talent. Your way looks dim because the treasure is still encased: worth no one has recognized waits for the discerning craftsman to cut the stone. Do not doubt the goal — doubt only shortcuts. Keep polishing your craft and seek the one who can judge jade; when that meeting comes, position and reward arrive together.", aspects: ["Worth the wait", "Find the judge", "Uncovered in time", "Ease returns"] },
    { no: 33, grade: "中签", titleZh: "咬金聘仁贵", title: "Yaojin Recruits Rengui", poemZh: "内藏无价宝和珍\n得玉何须外界寻\n不如等待高人识\n宽心犹且更宽心", poem: "Within is stored a treasure beyond price;\nHaving found the jade, why search outside?\nBetter to wait until a master recognizes it —\nAn easy heart, and still more ease.", meaning: "Cheng Yaojin rode out to recruit the overlooked Xue Rengui. What you need is already in your keeping, so the hunt outside only scatters your strength. Wait instead for the person of insight who can name the jade's worth — recommendation outlasts self-promotion. Loosen your grip, then loosen it again: calm is part of the strategy. Matters conclude; money grows slowly.", aspects: ["Calm brings match", "Await the judge", "Grows slowly", "At ease"] },
    { no: 34, grade: "中签", titleZh: "桃园结义", title: "The Oath of the Peach Garden", poemZh: "行藏出入礼义恭\n言必忠良信必从\n心不了然且静澈\n光明红日正当中", poem: "In conduct, in company, courteous and right;\nWords loyal and good, and trust follows them.\nWhere the heart is not yet clear, let it grow still and limpid —\nThe bright red sun stands at mid-sky.", meaning: "Liu Bei, Guan Yu, and Zhang Fei swore brotherhood beneath the peach blossoms — sincerity that planted an empire. Conduct yourself with courtesy and speak with loyalty; trust accrues like interest, and partnership holds. When motives blur, do not force a decision: let the heart settle until it is transparent, then act in the open daylight. Union is blessed; steady effort carries.", aspects: ["Sworn bonds", "Loyalty wins", "Steady gains", "Sunlit health"] },
    { no: 35, grade: "中签", titleZh: "唐僧取经", title: "Tang Monk Fetches the Scriptures", poemZh: "衣冠重整旧家风\n道是无穹却有功\n扫却当途荆棘刺\n三人约议再和同", poem: "Robes and cap renewed, the old family ways restored;\nSay it is heaven's vault — yet it is merit.\nSweep the brambles and thorns from the road ahead,\nThree companions consult and renew their accord.", meaning: "The Tang monk crossed ten thousand miles for the scriptures — no trial, no sutra. What looks like the empty vault of heaven is real merit in the making: restore discipline at home, clear the thorns from the road, and keep your small company in accord. Renovate before expanding. Once the path is swept, the journey resumes; a stalled romance or venture realigns after honest talk.", aspects: ["Renew the bond", "Rebuild first", "Swept, then gain", "Discipline heals"] },
    { no: 36, grade: "中签", titleZh: "湘子遇宾", title: "Xiangzi Meets the Immortal Guest", poemZh: "眼前病讼不须忧\n宝地资财尽可求\n恰似猿猴金锁脱\n自归山洞去来悠", poem: "Present illness and lawsuits — no need to worry;\nOn chosen ground, wealth may well be sought.\nJust so the golden lock slips off the monkey,\nAnd it returns to its mountain cave, free to come and go.", meaning: "Han Xiangzi met his immortal guest and turned from the world's tether. The ailments and disputes before your eyes will ease of themselves; on your present ground, resources can honestly be sought. Like the monkey whose golden lock falls away, you are being released into roomier days — return to your own mountain, keep your own rhythm, and freedom restores both appetite and health.", aspects: ["Freed to choose", "Thrives at home", "Fair rewards", "Recovery near"] },
    { no: 37, grade: "中签", titleZh: "李靖归山", title: "Li Jing Returns to the Mountain", poemZh: "欲待身安动泰时\n风中灯烛不相宜\n不如收拾深堂坐\n庶免光摇静处明", poem: "You would wait for full health and flourishing times;\nBut a lamp in the wind is not the place for it.\nBetter to gather in and sit in the deep hall —\nSpared the flicker, it shines bright where it is still.", meaning: "Li Jing, his work done, withdrew to the mountain. Like a candle flame in the wind, plans made amid commotion gutter however worthy they are. This is a season for consolidation, not expansion: step back to the sheltered hall, secure what flickers, and let brightness recover in stillness. Ventures that must move should wait for calm weather; health improves through rest, not resolve.", aspects: ["Sheltered union", "Withdraw, then move", "Guard the flame", "Rest cures"] },
    { no: 38, grade: "下签", titleZh: "何文秀遇难", title: "He Wenxiu Meets Peril", poemZh: "月照天书静处期\n忽遭云雾又昏迷\n宽心祈待云霞散\n此时更改好施为", poem: "Moonlight falls on heaven's letter, awaited in stillness;\nThen sudden clouds and fog bury it in dark.\nBroaden the heart and pray the mists disperse —\nWhen that hour comes, alter course and act.", meaning: "He Wenxiu suffered unjust persecution before vindication. The letter you awaited under moonlight has been fogged over: clarity turns to confusion, and a promising matter goes dark. This is obstruction, not ruin. Loosen your grip, keep faith, and wait for the clouds to break — pressing forward now only wastes strength. Once light returns, change your approach and act; love and fortune revive with the sky.", aspects: ["Fogged, wait clear", "Stalled, keep faith", "Delayed, then opens", "Pray and rest"] },
    { no: 39, grade: "下签", titleZh: "姜女寻夫", title: "Meng Jiangnü Seeks Her Husband", poemZh: "天边消息实难思\n切莫多心望强求\n若把石头磨作镜\n曾知枉费己功夫", poem: "News from the sky's edge is truly hard to fathom;\nDo not overthink it or strive to force it.\nGrind a stone in hope of making a mirror,\nAnd know at last your labor was in vain.", meaning: "Meng Jiangnü walked to the Great Wall for her husband and found grief — pursuit pressed past its season. The tidings you await from afar cannot be reasoned into being, and striving harder only grinds stone into a mirror that reflects nothing. Release the unreachable, keep the attainable: ordinary work still rewards. What must come will come by itself; what will not, no toil can fetch.", aspects: ["Release the chase", "Vain if forced", "Cut the loss", "Ease the strain"] },
    { no: 40, grade: "中签", titleZh: "武则天登位", title: "Wu Zetian Takes the Throne", poemZh: "红轮西坠兔东升\n阴长阳消百事亨\n是若女人宜望用\n增添财禄福其心", poem: "The red wheel sinks west, the hare climbs east;\nYin waxes, yang wanes — a hundred matters prosper.\nIf a woman holds the hope, the way opens wide,\nWith added wealth and rank to glad her heart.", meaning: "Wu Zetian rose where no woman had ruled. The great cycle is turning: what depended on others' favor now depends on your own hand, and enterprises move from darkness toward the light. For women especially, this is a season of recognized authority — step forward and take the helm. Fortunes and income both increase. Whatever your situation, let competence, not deference, speak.", aspects: ["Rising favor", "Take the helm", "Fortunes grow", "Radiant strength"] },
    { no: 41, grade: "中签", titleZh: "董卓收吕布", title: "Dong Zhuo Takes in Lü Bu", poemZh: "无限好言君记取\n却为认贼将作子\n莫贪眼下有些甜\n更虑他年前样看", poem: "Of endless fine words, mark well these:\nYou have hailed a thief and made him a son.\nCovet not the sweetness in front of your eyes;\nLook ahead, and see the pattern of former years.", meaning: "Dong Zhuo adopted the treacherous Lü Bu and was destroyed by him. Someone charming is near whose loyalty has already shown cracks: flattering words, borrowed sweetness, a debt of favor you did not weigh. Enjoy the honey if you must, but record the pattern — this story has played before and its ending is written. Put distance, not hope, between you. Choose old, proven friends over new brilliance.", aspects: ["Flattery, no trust", "Vet new allies", "Sweet now, costly", "Guard the strain"] },
    { no: 42, grade: "上签", titleZh: "目莲救母", title: "Mulian Rescues His Mother", poemZh: "君皇圣后终为恩\n复待祈禳无损增\n一切有情皆受用\n人间天上得期亨", poem: "Sovereign and sage queen, in the end, are grace;\nKeep praying and fasting — nothing lost, all gained.\nEvery sentient thing shares in the blessing;\nOn earth and in heaven, the season runs prosperous.", meaning: "Mulian descended into the hells out of filial love and freed his mother — devotion that moves heaven. Your petitions are heard: prayers and good works done now lose nothing and quietly accrue. This sign rewards kindness extended to others; every creature touched by it shares the gain. Family luck brightens, help arrives from above expectation, and long-blocked matters find their hour. Give, and be patient.", aspects: ["Devotion blessed", "Heaven assists", "Blessings accrue", "Prayer restores"] },
    { no: 43, grade: "上签", titleZh: "行者得道", title: "The Traveler Attains the Dao", poemZh: "天地变通万物全\n自营自养自安然\n生罗万象皆精彩\n事事如心谢圣贤", poem: "Heaven and earth shift into harmony; all things are whole;\nSelf-tended, self-nourished, you are at peace.\nThe living net of the myriad forms shines forth in splendor —\nEach matter as the heart would wish: give thanks to the sages.", meaning: "The wandering practitioner came home to the Dao — the world, at last, complete. After long circulation, your fortunes have found their channel: self-managed work now sustains itself, and what you build with your own hands stands secure. Everything in view takes on its color; plans fall out as the heart desires. This is ripeness, not luck — thank your teachers, guard your conduct, and enjoy the season.", aspects: ["Fulfilled union", "Self-made success", "All in order", "Wholly well"] },
    { no: 44, grade: "中签", titleZh: "姜维邓艾斗阵", title: "Jiang Wei and Deng Ai Match Formations", poemZh: "棋逢敌手着相宜\n黑白盘中未决时\n皆因一着知胜败\n须教自有好推宜", poem: "Chess meets its equal — each move well matched;\nIn the black-and-white board the game hangs unresolved.\nOn a single move the victory or defeat will turn,\nSo think your own best sequence through.", meaning: "Jiang Wei and Deng Ai fenced with formations, evenly matched. You face a rival of your own caliber: the contest is genuine, the outcome genuinely open, and neither bluff nor luck will decide it. Study the board yourself rather than borrowing another's line — one considered move now outweighs ten hasty ones. Marriage or partnership holds only after honest negotiation. Calm calculation is your winning piece.", aspects: ["Even match", "Outcalculate", "One move decides", "Stay composed"] },
    { no: 45, grade: "上签", titleZh: "仁宗认母", title: "Renzong Recognizes His Mother", poemZh: "温柔自古胜刚强\n积善之门大吉昌\n若是有人占此卦\n宛如正渴遇瑶浆", poem: "Gentleness has ever conquered hardness;\nThe household that stores up goodness meets great fortune.\nWhoever draws this hexagram of ours —\nIt is like jade nectar found in raging thirst.", meaning: "Emperor Renzong recognized the mother he had lost — truth reunited with love. Yielding wins where force fails: soften the hard words, and doors that argument could not open swing wide. The goodness this household has banked is now paying interest — fortune rises in every quarter. Whatever the longing, it is answered like cool nectar in fierce thirst. Receive it with gratitude and keep storing the good.", aspects: ["Gentle reunion", "Goodness rewarded", "Nectar in thirst", "Refreshed health"] },
    { no: 46, grade: "中签", titleZh: "渭水钓鱼", title: "Fishing at the Wei River", poemZh: "劝君耐守旧生涯\n把定心肠勿起歹\n直待有人轻着力\n枯枝老树再生花", poem: "I counsel you: patiently keep your old livelihood;\nHold your heart firm, let no crooked thought rise.\nWait until someone lends a light hand —\nThen the withered branch, the old tree, flowers again.", meaning: "Jiang Taigong fished the Wei with a straight hook, waiting for his hour. Old trades and old positions feel barren now, but uprooting them in restlessness is the one real danger. Hold the line you know, keep your conscience clean, and let the season turn: a light push from the right person brings dead wood into flower. What you tend faithfully revives; what you abandon now stays lost.", aspects: ["Keep old ties", "Hold your post", "Slow but sure", "Old tree flowers"] },
    { no: 47, grade: "上签", titleZh: "梁灏登科", title: "Liang Hao Passes the Examination", poemZh: "锦上添花色愈鲜\n运来禄马喜双全\n时人莫恨功名晚\n一举登科四海传", poem: "Brocade gains its flower, and the colors grow brighter still;\nWhen fortune comes, salary and steed arrive — a double joy.\nLet no one resent that fame arrives late:\nOne pass at the examination, and the four seas carry your name.", meaning: "Liang Hao took the highest degree at eighty-two — late, then legendary. Your season has turned: advantages stack upon advantages, and what was long delayed now arrives doubled. Do not resent the years it took; preparation plus timing equals renown. Take the decisive examination, launch the venture, make the proposal — one bold stroke now travels far. A late rise outshines an early one.", aspects: ["Double joy", "Late fame, bright", "Doubled gains", "Strong season"] },
    { no: 48, grade: "中签", titleZh: "韩信挂帅", title: "Han Xin Takes Command", poemZh: "鹍鸟秋来化作鹏\n好游快乐喜飞腾\n翱翔万里云霄去\n余外诸禽总不能", poem: "The kun bird, autumn come, transforms into the roc;\nDelightedly it wanders, joyous in its flight,\nSoaring ten thousand miles into the clouded sky —\nNo other bird among them can do the like.", meaning: "Han Xin, once humiliated, became grand marshal. Like the vast kun-fish changing into the roc at autumn's call, a long-hidden capacity is molting into its great form. This is expansion season: travel, move, launch — the wide sky is genuinely yours, and smaller rivals cannot follow you there. Enjoy the ascent without arrogance; the climb from low places taught you what rank never will. Health rides the lift.", aspects: ["Soaring match", "Rise and expand", "Big game now", "Rides the lift"] },
    { no: 49, grade: "中签", titleZh: "王祥求鲤", title: "Wang Xiang Seeks the Carp", poemZh: "天寒地冻水成冰\n何须贪吝取功名\n只好守己静处坐\n待时兴变自然明", poem: "Sky cold, earth frozen, the waters turn to ice;\nWhy grasp and begrudge in pursuit of rank?\nBest keep to yourself, sitting in a quiet place,\nAnd wait: the turn will come, and all grow clear.", meaning: "Wang Xiang lay on the ice to fetch carp for his stepmother — devotion that melted the river. Conditions are frozen: pushing for advancement in a hard season costs more than it returns. Do not begrudge what others gain now; sit still, keep your integrity, and let the thaw do its work. When the season shifts, the way opens without force. Patient devotion is banked, not wasted.", aspects: ["Ice thaws late", "Outlast the frost", "Hold, don't chase", "Warm care"] },
    { no: 50, grade: "中签", titleZh: "陶朱归五湖", title: "Tao Zhu Returns to the Five Lakes", poemZh: "五湖四海任君行\n高挂帆蓬自在撑\n若得顺风随即至\n满船宝贝喜层层", poem: "The five lakes and four seas — go where you will;\nHoist the sail high and ply it at ease.\nCatch a fair wind, and you arrive straightaway,\nThe ship loaded with treasure, joy stacked layer on layer.", meaning: "Fan Li, richest of merchants, left the court for the five lakes and traded freely. Boundaries are open to you now: move, travel, deal across distances — the sail is yours to hoist. When the fair wind finds you, arrival is quick and the hold fills layer by layer. The caveat is weather: profits come with the wind, not against it. Choose the timing as carefully as the course.", aspects: ["Sails together", "Voyage rewards", "Fair wind profits", "Wind-fresh health"] },
    { no: 51, grade: "上签", titleZh: "孔明入川", title: "Kongming Enters Shu", poemZh: "夏日炎天日最长\n人人愁热闷非常\n天地也解知人意\n熏风拂拂自然凉", poem: "High summer, blazing sky — the days at their longest;\nEveryone frets at heat beyond bearing.\nYet heaven and earth know the heart's desire:\nA warm south breeze, and coolness comes of itself.", meaning: "Kongming entered Shu and order followed him. The pressure has peaked: everyone around you is wilting in the same heat, and the discomfort is general, not a judgment on you. Relief is nearer than it feels — conditions themselves are about to ease, like a breeze arriving on its own. Bear the last stretch; let the season turn. Affairs, feelings, and health all cool for the better.", aspects: ["Warm, then cool", "Ease follows effort", "Steady inflow", "Breeze restores"] },
    { no: 52, grade: "中签", titleZh: "太白醉捞明月", title: "Taibai, Drunk, Scoops at the Moon", poemZh: "水中捉月费功夫\n费尽功夫却又无\n莫说闲言并乱语\n枉劳心力强身枯", poem: "Seizing the moon in the water costs much labor;\nSpend all that labor — and still there is nothing.\nDo not speak idle words and tangled talk;\nVainly wearing heart and strength, the body dries up.", meaning: "Li Bai, drunk, reached for the moon in the river and drowned in the reaching. Some prize you pursue is a reflection: no striving will grasp it, and the strain is hollowing you out. Name it honestly — a person, a profit, a vindication — and stop paying for it. Talk about it is as wasted as effort. Redirect labor toward substance, and the body recovers too.", aspects: ["Moon in water", "Cut illusions", "Chase nothing", "Rest the strain"] },
    { no: 53, grade: "中签", titleZh: "刘备招亲", title: "Liu Bei Wins a Bride", poemZh: "失意番成得意时\n龙吟虎啸两相宜\n青天自有通霄路\n许我功名再有期", poem: "Disappointment turns into its opposite — the hour of success;\nDragon hums, tiger roars, and the two are well matched.\nThe blue heaven holds its own high-road through the clouds;\nRank and renown are promised me once more.", meaning: "Liu Bei sailed into a trap and came home with a bride — setback flipped into fortune. What failed is turning into what fulfills: a partnership in which both voices sound — dragon and tiger — is the right match, not a quiet one. Your road through the clouds was never closed, only unmapped; another term of achievement is already scheduled. Move with the turn, not against it.", aspects: ["Dragon meets tiger", "Reversal to rise", "Returns on term", "Roaring strength"] },
    { no: 54, grade: "下签", titleZh: "马超追曹", title: "Ma Chao Pursues Cao", poemZh: "梦中得宝醒来无\n自谓南山只是锄\n若问婚姻并问病\n别寻来路为相扶", poem: "Treasure gained in a dream is gone at waking;\nYou called it South Mountain — it was only a hoe.\nAsk of marriage, ask of illness:\nSeek another road, and find someone to lean on.", meaning: "Ma Chao chased Cao Cao through victory into ambush and lost nearly everything. The prize felt certain in the dream of pursuit; awake, the chest is empty. Overconfidence after a first success is the trap here. For marriage and health especially, do not press the current line — change the approach, change the adviser, take a different road entirely. What remains is rescued by adjustment, not by doubling down.", aspects: ["Change course", "Curb the chase", "Seek new outlet", "New healer, care"] },
    { no: 55, grade: "中签", titleZh: "周武王登位", title: "King Wu of Zhou Takes the Throne", poemZh: "父贤传子子传孙\n衣食丰隆只靠天\n堂上椿萱人快乐\n饥饭渴饮困时眠", poem: "A worthy father hands to son, the son to grandson;\nRaiment and rice abound — by heaven's grace alone.\nIn the hall, parents rejoice;\nHungry, eat; thirsty, drink; weary, sleep.", meaning: "King Wu inherited a mandate built by three generations. This sign is inheritance and continuation: what your elders established passes into your keeping, and the provision is ample so long as you honor its source. Ordinary contentment is the instruction — eat when hungry, drink when thirsty, sleep when weary — rather than feverish ambition. Tend the elders in the hall, keep the household rhythm — the line holds rich.", aspects: ["House of joy", "Keep the charge", "Ample, given", "Eat, sleep well"] },
    { no: 56, grade: "中签", titleZh: "禄山谋反", title: "An Lushan Rebels", poemZh: "滩小石溪流水响\n风清明月贵人忙\n路须借问何方去\n莫取林中花草香", poem: "A small rapid, a stony brook, the water sounding;\nWind clear, moon bright, yet worthies hurry past.\nAsk your way — which direction to go;\nDo not pluck the fragrant flowers of the wood.", meaning: "An Lushan's rebellion looked promising and ended in ruin — the flower off the path. Your setting is pleasant but unsettled: clear moon, noisy shallows, everyone busy and no one certain. Before moving, ask directions frankly of those who know; guesswork on a shifting road is how travelers are lost. Sweet temptations beside the path — quick profits, flattering offers — leave them unpicked. Ask, then walk.", aspects: ["Ask elders first", "Ask, then move", "No roadside plucking", "Calm nights"] },
    { no: 57, grade: "中签", titleZh: "董仲寻亲", title: "Dong Zhong Seeks His Kin", poemZh: "说是说非风过耳\n好衣好禄自然丰\n君莫记取当年事\n汝意还如我意同", poem: "Talk of right and wrong — wind past the ear;\nFine clothes and fine salary come of themselves in time.\nDo not keep dwelling on the affairs of past years;\nYour wish and mine, after all, are one.", meaning: "Dong Zhong searched for years for his lost parents. The chatter about who was right no longer matters — let it pass your ear as wind. Provision is gathering on its own, so the past need not be relitigated. What was severed can be rejoined when both sides quietly want the same thing: state it once, then be patient. Reunion favors the one who lets go of the ledger.", aspects: ["Old tie renews", "Wind past ears", "Gathers itself", "Wind clears mind"] },
    { no: 58, grade: "中签", titleZh: "文王问卜", title: "King Wen Consults the Oracle", poemZh: "直言说话君须记\n莫在他乡求别艺\n切须守己旧生涯\n除是其余都不利", poem: "Words spoken straight — you must remember them:\nDo not go seeking other arts in other lands.\nHold strictly to your own established trade,\nFor every other way will only bring you loss.", meaning: "King Wen asked the oracle and got a blunt answer. Here is yours: the opportunity glittering in another city or trade is not for you — the cost hides behind the shine. Your old craft and old connections are the profitable ground, and switching now is the identifiable risk. Stay with what you know, deepen it, and let others chase the novelty. Unglamorous, but true.", aspects: ["Stay with known", "Keep your post", "Old trade pays", "Home remedies"] },
    { no: 59, grade: "中签", titleZh: "张良隐山", title: "Zhang Liang Withdraws to the Mountains", poemZh: "直上重楼去藏身\n四围荆棘绕为林\n天高君命长和短\n得一番成失二人", poem: "Straight up the storied tower you go to hide yourself;\nOn every side thorn-brakes circle into forest.\nHeaven is high; your fate runs long or short —\nOne affair is won, but two persons are lost.", meaning: "Zhang Liang withdrew at the peak of triumph, knowing when to leave. The achievement you seek requires climbing exposed heights surrounded by thorns — success will cost you: a partnership, perhaps a friendship, perhaps more than you priced. Weigh what winning is worth before you climb; heaven does not guarantee length of days to the ambitious. Some versions of success are failures at a higher altitude. Choose your thorns consciously.", aspects: ["Costs two bonds", "Weigh the price", "Gain costs loss", "Mind the strain"] },
    { no: 60, grade: "下签", titleZh: "赤壁鏖兵", title: "Battle of the Red Cliffs", poemZh: "抱薪救火大皆燃\n烧遍三千亦复然\n若问荣华并出入\n不如收拾枉劳心", poem: "Carrying faggots to quench the fire — all the greater it burns;\nThree thousand acres scorched, and still it spreads.\nAsk of glory and of goings-out:\nBetter gather everything in than toil in vain.", meaning: "The Red Cliffs burned an armada that trusted its own numbers. Your method is the fuel: every added effort feeds the very fire you mean to put out — in a dispute, a venture, an ailment. Stop carrying wood. Ambition and travel should both be folded away for now; retreat is the winning move. Salvage what is portable, bank your strength, and let the field cool before you return.", aspects: ["Stand back", "Retreat wins", "Cut losses now", "Cool the field"] },
    { no: 61, grade: "中签", titleZh: "苏小妹难夫", title: "Su Xiaomei Tests Her Groom", poemZh: "日落吟诗月下歌\n逢场作戏笑呵呵\n相逢会遇难藏避\n唱彩齐唱连理罗", poem: "At sunset, chanting poems, singing beneath the moon;\nMeeting the occasion in play, laughing heartily;\nWhen kindred spirits meet, there is no hiding it —\nChorus upon chorus sings the twining vines of love.", meaning: "Su Xiaomei tested her groom with verse rounds before saying yes. This sign is courtship as festival: banter, verse, gathering occasions where masks slip and true minds show. If a bond is forming, let it surface in the open — games and gatherings reveal what solemn interviews conceal. Joy now is genuine but still playful; keep it light and let affection declare itself. What begins in shared laughter lasts.", aspects: ["Laughter bonds", "Light success", "Gather, then gain", "Light heart"] },
    { no: 62, grade: "中签", titleZh: "唐僧得道", title: "Tang Monk Attains the Way", poemZh: "晨昏全赖佛扶持\n须是逢危却不危\n若得贵人相引处\n那时财帛亦相随", poem: "Dawn and dusk, all rests on the Buddha's upholding;\nThough you meet danger, yet you shall not be harmed.\nShould a noble one point out the path ahead,\nThen wealth and goods will follow in train.", meaning: "The Tang monk reached the sutras through perils that never actually touched him. Morning and evening, a quiet protection carries your undertakings: dangers will arise and pass without landing, provided you keep faith and routine. Your part is to stay worthy of guidance — honest, observant, grateful — and to accept the helping hand when offered. Once the right person leads the way, resources follow almost as an afterthought.", aspects: ["Guarded union", "Safe through perils", "Follows guidance", "Held at dawn"] },
    { no: 63, grade: "中签", titleZh: "女娲氏炼石", title: "Nüwa Refines the Stone", poemZh: "昔然行船失了针\n今朝依旧海中寻\n若然寻得原针在\n也费工夫也费心", poem: "Long ago, sailing, you lost the needle;\nToday as ever you search for it in the sea.\nShould you find the very needle again,\nStill it costs you labor, still it costs you heart.", meaning: "Nüwa smelted stones to mend heaven itself — vast repair done twice over. Something small was lost in a vast place: the search costs more than the object, and even success arrives only with heavy effort. Ask whether the lost needle is worth the ocean. If it is a matter of honor or love, search deliberately; if of profit, the ledger already says no. Repair what is truly broken.", aspects: ["Search if worthy", "Heavy effort", "Costs exceed gains", "Slow mending"] },
    { no: 64, grade: "下签", titleZh: "马前覆水", title: "Spilled Water Before the Horse", poemZh: "游鱼却在碧波池\n撞遭罗网四边围\n思量无计番身出\n事到头来惹事非", poem: "The swimming fish, at ease in the jade-green pool,\nSudden strikes the net on every side enclosed;\nPonder as it may, no way to turn and escape —\nThe affair at its end breeds more affairs of harm.", meaning: "Zhu Maichen's wife divorced him in his poverty; when he rose, the spilled water could not be gathered again. Comfortable waters have turned treacherous: entanglements — legal, financial, relational — close from four sides, and cleverness alone cannot slip the mesh. Do not struggle in ways that attract more trouble; seek a mediator, simplify, and accept slower extraction. Lesson for later: do not pour the water.", aspects: ["Netted, seek help", "Disentangle slow", "Loss, cut clean", "Unwind gently"] },
    { no: 65, grade: "下签", titleZh: "孙膑困庞涓", title: "Sun Bin Traps Pang Juan", poemZh: "眼前欢喜未为欢\n亦不危时亦不安\n割肉补疮为甚事\n不如守旧待时光", poem: "The joy before your eyes is not yet joy;\nNeither in danger, yet never at ease.\nCutting flesh to patch a wound — to what end?\nBetter keep the old way and wait upon time.", meaning: "Sun Bin feigned weakness while Pang Juan walked into the trap — apparent delight concealing distress. The present pleasure is borrowed against later pain: not yet disaster, but nowhere near peace. Stop paying today's bills with tomorrow's flesh — the refinancing, the overwork, the shortcut that wounds. Hold the old routine, however dull, and let time rebalance the books. The wound heals only when the knife stops.", aspects: ["Joy on credit", "Hold old ways", "Stop the bleeding", "Rest, don't patch"] },
    { no: 66, grade: "下签", titleZh: "霸王被困", title: "The Hegemon Besieged", poemZh: "路险马乏人行急\n失群军卒困相当\n滩高风浪船棹破\n日暮花残天降霜", poem: "The road is perilous, the horse spent, the travelers hurrying;\nTroops scattered, the stragglers equally trapped.\nOn the high shallows wind and waves shatter the oars;\nDay fades, flowers wither, and frost descends from the sky.", meaning: "Xiang Yu, unbeatable in the field, was caught at Gaixia with no road left. Pressure comes from every side at once: the mount exhausted, the path dangerous, the company scattered, the boat's oar broken at the shoal, frost at dusk. Do not force a crossing now — in career, romance, or health. Conserve, rally the closest companions, and wait for first light. Sieges end for those still standing.", aspects: ["Frost, then thaw", "Hold, don't cross", "Scattered, gather", "Warmth, conserve"] },
    { no: 67, grade: "上签", titleZh: "金精试窦儿", title: "A Golden Spirit Tests the Dou Child", poemZh: "一条金线秤君心\n无减无增无重轻\n为人平生心正直\n文章全具艺光明", poem: "A single thread of gold weighs your heart;\nNothing added, nothing taken, neither heavy nor light.\nFor one whose life is upright and true,\nThe writing is complete, the arts shine bright.", meaning: "The Dou child passed the golden spirit's testing and inherited the mantle. The scale in this sign is invisible but accurate: character is being weighed, and consistency — the same person in dark and light — is the measure. Live evenly and your work ripens: writing complete, craft luminous, reputation unforced. Examinations and judgments of every kind favor you, for nothing is hidden. Stay level; the balance is yours.", aspects: ["True balance", "Even, complete", "Earned, steady", "Sound and bright"] },
    { no: 68, grade: "中签", titleZh: "郭汾阳祝寿", title: "Guo Fenyang Celebrates a Birthday", poemZh: "门廷吉庆喜非常\n积善之门大吉昌\n婚姻田蚕诸事遂\n病逢妙药即安康", poem: "Before the gate and court, festivity beyond the ordinary;\nThe household that stores up goodness meets great fortune.\nMarriage, fields, and silkworms — every matter succeeds;\nThe sick, meeting a wondrous medicine, are well again.", meaning: "Guo Ziyi, the Guo Fenyang of the title, celebrated birthdays past eighty — fortune that accumulated from accumulated virtue. Festivity at your gate is earned, not random: the goodness this house has stored is now compounding. Marriages proceed, harvests and enterprises come in, and an illness finally meets its true remedy. Attend the celebration, thank the elders, and keep storing the good — the pattern guarantees the next.", aspects: ["Household joy", "All succeeds", "Harvests come in", "Right medicine"] },
    { no: 69, grade: "中签", titleZh: "梅开二度", title: "The Plum Blooms Twice", poemZh: "冬来岭上一枝梅\n叶落枝枯终不摧\n但得阳春悄急至\n依然还我作花魁", poem: "Winter comes, and on the ridge a single plum;\nLeaves fallen, branches withered, yet never broken.\nOnly let warm spring steal swiftly in —\nAnd once more it stands, the queen of flowers.", meaning: "The plum that flowered once bloomed again — revival after apparent death. You have been stripped: leaves gone, season hostile, yet the root never broke. What looks finished is dormant. When the warm weather arrives — and it will arrive quietly, suddenly — you return as chief of the flowers, not as a survivor. Meanwhile, withstand; do not confuse bare branches with dead ones. Second bloom is the theme.", aspects: ["Blooms again", "Revives in spring", "Returns with spring", "Root holds firm"] },
    { no: 70, grade: "下签", titleZh: "李密反唐", title: "Li Mi Rebels Against Tang", poemZh: "朝朝恰似采花蜂\n飞出西南又走东\n春尽花残无觅处\n此心不变旧行踪", poem: "Day after day, just like the honeybee among flowers,\nFlying out to the southwest, then away to the east;\nSpring ends, the blossoms wither, nowhere to seek them —\nYet this heart unchanged keeps its former course.", meaning: "Li Mi kept switching allegiances until no side would have him. Your busy harvesting — project to project, person to person — assumes the flowers never end. They will. When the season closes, the wanderer has neither store nor hive. Loyalty to one good line of work now outweighs three flirtations; a fixed heart at least keeps its old tracks. Choose the flower you can keep.", aspects: ["Settle on one", "Stay the course", "Store, don't roam", "Fixed routine"] },
    { no: 71, grade: "中签", titleZh: "文君访相如", title: "Wenjun Visits Xiangru", poemZh: "认知苍龙下九衢\n女子当年嫁二夫\n自是一弓架两箭\n欲恐龙马不安居", poem: "Behold the grey dragon descending the nine thoroughfares;\nA woman, in her day, wedded to two husbands.\nIt is one bow set with two arrows —\nAnd one may fear the dragon-horse will not settle.", meaning: "Zhuo Wenjun eloped to Sima Xiangru — a second match after widowhood, and the right one. This sign sanctions an unconventional union or arrangement: a relationship renewed, a career changed, two lines drawn on one bow. What matters is honesty about the doubling, for a bow strung with two arrows can strain. Where the structure is openly agreed, it holds; where it hides, the strong horse grows restless. Proceed candidly.", aspects: ["Second match", "Two lines drawn", "Split attention", "Candor steadies"] },
    { no: 72, grade: "中签", titleZh: "王莽求贤", title: "Wang Mang Seeks Worthies", poemZh: "养蜂须用求他蜜\n只怕遭触尾上针\n须是眼前有异路\n暗里深如荆棘林", poem: "You keep bees in hope of harvesting their honey,\nYet fear to meet the sting upon the tail.\nBefore your eyes there is indeed an unusual road,\nBut hidden away it runs deep as a thorn-brake wood.", meaning: "Wang Mang recruited talent to consolidate a usurpation — sweetness sought with a sting attached. The offer before you carries both: real honey and a real stinger, and pretending otherwise is how hands get hurt. There is a different road, but it is not the marked one; it runs through thorn-brakes where progress is slow and scratched. Choose knowingly: sweet with stings, or honest and thorny.", aspects: ["Stings hidden", "Mind the sting", "Honey with risk", "Careful handling"] },
    { no: 73, grade: "上签", titleZh: "陈桥兵变", title: "The Mutiny at Chenqiao", poemZh: "春来雷震百虫鸣\n番身一转离泥中\n始知出入还来往\n一朝变化便成龙", poem: "Spring comes; thunder rolls, and the hundred insects cry;\nOne turn, one flip, and they leave the mud behind.\nThen you know the going out and coming in again —\nIn a single morning's change, you become a dragon.", meaning: "At Chenqiao the soldiers draped the yellow robe on their general, and a commoner's dynasty began. The thunder of spring is waking everything at once: your dormant period ends not gradually but in a flip — one turn and the mud is behind you. Doors once battered in vain now swing both ways. The change may arrive as others lift you. Be ready to rise when the robe lands.", aspects: ["Thunderous union", "One flip, rising", "Doors reopen", "Vigor returns"] },
    { no: 74, grade: "下签", titleZh: "秦败擒三帅", title: "Qin Defeated, Three Generals Taken", poemZh: "似鹄飞来自入笼\n欲得番身却不通\n南北东西都难出\n此卦诚恐恨无穹", poem: "Like the swan that flew — and flew into a cage;\nIt longs to turn about, but there is no way through.\nSouth, north, east, west — no exit anywhere;\nTruly this hexagram is feared: regret without end.", meaning: "Qin's three captured generals walked free into a trap of their own choosing. Like a swan that flew itself into a cage, the confinement here grew out of earlier choices — commitments, contracts, entanglements accepted one by one. Struggling only proves the cage. Submit to a season of stillness: meet the obligations, learn the lesson, and let time and conduct loosen the latch. Sign nothing while caged.", aspects: ["Caged, be still", "Trapped, wait out", "Bound, untie slow", "Stillness heals"] },
    { no: 75, grade: "中签", titleZh: "伍员夜出昭关", title: "Wu Yuan Flees Zhaoguan by Night", poemZh: "恰如抱虎过高山\n战战竞竞胆碎寒\n不觉忽然从好事\n切须保守一身安", poem: "It is just like carrying a tiger across high mountains,\nTrembling, trembling, gall shivered to ice;\nThen, all unnoticed, good comes of the affair —\nOnly be sure to keep your one self safe.", meaning: "Wu Yuan escaped Zhaoguan by night with his hair turned white — deliverance through terror. You are holding a tiger: obligations or dangers that must be carried, not dropped, across the mountain of this season. Fear is appropriate; paralysis and recklessness are not. Move at night, move carefully, ask help discreetly — the crossing keeps succeeding against the odds. Once through, guard the health this passage cost you.", aspects: ["Dangerous, guarded", "Careful crossing", "Risky but passable", "Guard yourself"] },
    { no: 76, grade: "中签", titleZh: "洪武看牛", title: "Hongwu Tends the Buffalo", poemZh: "鱼龙混杂意相同\n耐守深潭待运通\n不觉一朝头耸出\n禹门一跳过龙宫", poem: "Fish and dragon are mixed together, their intent the same;\nPatiently keep the deep pool and wait for fortune's flow.\nUnnoticed, one morning the head rises clear —\nOne leap at Yu's Gate, and past the dragon palace.", meaning: "Zhu Yuanzhang herded buffalo before founding a dynasty — history's lowest start. In the mixed crowd, the undistinguished and the destined look alike; the pool's depth is your protection, not your ceiling. Keep the humble post, keep the discipline, and let fortune's current arrive. When it does, the rise is sudden — head above water, one leap through the Dragon Gate. Obscurity is preparation, not verdict.", aspects: ["Hidden among many", "Hold the pool", "Leaps the gate", "Deep water calm"] },
    { no: 77, grade: "中签", titleZh: "捧璧归赵", title: "Returning the Jade to Zhao", poemZh: "梦中说得是多财\n声名云外终虚来\n水远山遥难信实\n贵人指点笑颜开", poem: "In dreams you speak of nothing but great wealth;\nFame beyond the clouds arrives in the end as mist.\nWaters far, mountains distant — hard to trust the news;\nA noble one's pointing finger, and the face opens in smiles.", meaning: "Lin Xiangru carried the priceless jade safely home through mortal danger. The wealth promised so vividly — in dreams, in rumor, from far away — is not yet money in the hand; distance feeds doubt, and cloud-fame casts no shadow. What turns this around is a trustworthy guide: find the person who knows the road and the buyer, and the smile returns. Verify first; celebrate when it is home.", aspects: ["Verify, then smile", "Guide unlocks it", "Distant, unproven", "Calm the worry"] },
    { no: 78, grade: "上签", titleZh: "临潼救驾", title: "Rescue at Lintong", poemZh: "冷水未烧白沸汤\n不寒不热有温凉\n要行天下无他事\n为有身中百艺强", poem: "Cold water, not yet boiled, and already a white-seething broth;\nNeither cold nor hot — a temperate warmth.\nTo travel the whole world needs nothing else:\nThe hundred arts within you are your strength.", meaning: "Qin Qiong rescued the emperor's carriage at Lintong with skill alone. Your position is neither frozen nor feverish — a workable temperature — and what makes you safe anywhere is the craft you carry in your own body. Artistry, plural: develop more than one competence, and no market, office, or crisis can strand you. Walk where you will; the hundred arts pay the toll. Health rests on the same balance.", aspects: ["Well tempered", "Skilled everywhere", "Craft earns tolls", "Balanced health"] },
    { no: 79, grade: "中签", titleZh: "暗扶倒铜旗", title: "Secretly Toppling the Bronze Banner", poemZh: "虚空结愿保平安\n保得身安愿不还\n莫忘神圣宜还了\n此知神语莫轻慢", poem: "In empty air you vowed a prayer for peace;\nPeace was granted — and the vow went unrepaid.\nForget not the sacred one; the vow should be settled —\nKnow the divine words; do not treat them lightly.", meaning: "Dark forces upheld the collapsing bronze banner unseen, and the general lived. Your safety through the recent passage was not luck alone — help arrived, visible or not, and a debt of gratitude remains open. Repayment need not be dramatic: a promise honored, a gift given, a thank-you said. The warning is precise: preserved people who forget their vows lose the protection that preserved them. Close the loop early.", aspects: ["Repay the vow", "Gratitude keeps grace", "Give back share", "Vow kept, well"] },
    { no: 80, grade: "上签", titleZh: "智远投军", title: "Zhiyuan Joins the Army", poemZh: "直上仙岩要学仙\n此知一旦帝王宣\n青天日月常明照\n心正声名四海传", poem: "Straight up the immortal cliff to study the immortal way;\nAnd know: one day the sovereign himself will call.\nBlue heaven's sun and moon shine constant and clear;\nHeart upright, your name is carried through the four seas.", meaning: "Liu Zhiyuan enlisted as a common soldier and rose to found a dynasty. The training you are climbing toward is not the end but the door: those who climb the cliff get summoned by the throne. Keep the heart upright; under constant light, reputations travel farther than résumés. Every part of this sign rises when the motive stays clean. Enroll; the summons follows.", aspects: ["Clean and bright", "Summoned upward", "Earned renown", "Sunlit health"] },
    { no: 81, grade: "上签", titleZh: "风送滕王阁", title: "Wind-Sent to Tengwang Pavilion", poemZh: "梧桐叶落秋将暮\n行客归程去似云\n谢得天公高着力\n顺风船载宝珍归", poem: "Wutong leaves fall; autumn nears its close;\nThe traveler's homeward road goes swift as cloud.\nThanks be to Heaven, exerting its power on high —\nA fair wind, and the boat carries treasure home.", meaning: "Wang Bo reached the Tengwang banquet because a lucky wind carried his boat — talent plus a tailwind. The year is late, the return overdue, but the closing season turns generous: what was scattered comes home in one load. The crucial factor arrives from above your calculations — a wind you did not purchase. So write the poem, thank heaven for the wind, and sail while it blows.", aspects: ["Wind-borne match", "Late, then splendid", "One cargo home", "Fresh wind health"] },
    { no: 82, grade: "中签", titleZh: "火烧葫芦谷", title: "Fire in the Gourd Valley", poemZh: "炎炎烈火焰连天\n焰里还生一朵莲\n到底得成终不害\n依然生叶长根枝", poem: "Blazing flames, fierce fire joining sky to sky;\nYet within the flame a lotus is born.\nIn the end it ripens and is never harmed —\nStill putting forth leaves, still growing root and branch.", meaning: "Zhuge Liang walked out of the burning Gourd Valley — and so, in legend, does Sima Yi. You are inside the fire: pressure or illness fierce enough to touch the sky. The lotus born in flame is the point — something in this ordeal is being tempered, not destroyed. Hold position through the burning; what emerges keeps its roots, grows its branches, marked by survival. No lasting harm is promised.", aspects: ["Lotus in fire", "Tempered, holds", "Grows through flame", "Unharmed at last"] },
    { no: 83, grade: "中签", titleZh: "李渊登位", title: "Li Yuan Takes the Throne", poemZh: "譬若初三四五缺\n半无半有未圆全\n等待十五良宵夜\n到处光明到处圆", poem: "It is like the moon at the third, fourth, fifth day —\nHalf absent, half present, not yet full and whole;\nWait for the fifteenth night, the fine full-moon eve,\nAnd everywhere is brightness, everywhere round.", meaning: "Li Yuan's dynasty began while rivals still stood — power that matured by the fifteenth night. Your matter is a waxing crescent: real, growing, but visibly incomplete, and the gap tempts you to force it. The moon needs no assistance to fill. Keep appointments, keep building, and let the cycle complete; on the night it rounds, brightness is everywhere at once. Everything here is a question of dates, not doubt.", aspects: ["Waxing toward full", "Waits for fullness", "Fills in time", "Rounding to health"] },
    { no: 84, grade: "下签", titleZh: "庄子试妻", title: "Zhuangzi Tests His Wife", poemZh: "因名丧德如何事\n切恐吉中变化凶\n酒醉不知何处去\n青松影里梦朦胧", poem: "For the sake of a name you lose virtue — what comes of that?\nFear most the good that turns to ill.\nDrunk with wine, unknowing where to go,\nIn the shadow of green pines, a dim and troubled dream.", meaning: "Zhuangzi faked death to test his wife; the marriage collapsed into the trap of suspicion. The warning: testing what should be trusted corrodes the very thing it means to secure. What looks auspicious can flip under this influence — mind the wine, the fog, the half-lit pines. If a bond has turned murky, do not stage experiments. Come out of the dream, sober up, and deal in daylight.", aspects: ["Trust, don't test", "Avoid schemes", "Flip risk, quit", "Sober the mind"] },
    { no: 85, grade: "中签", titleZh: "韩文公遇雪", title: "Han Wengong Meets the Snow", poemZh: "云开雾罩山前路\n万物圆中月再圆\n若得诗书沉梦醒\n贵人指引步天台", poem: "Clouds part, yet mist still veils the road before the mountain;\nIn the round of all things, the moon grows round once more.\nShould the dream of poetry and books grow deep — wake;\nA noble guide will lead your steps up Tiantai.", meaning: "Han Yu, banished to the snows of Lantian, turned back by weather and by mercy. The fog lifts but has not lifted: the mountain road stays hidden even as the moon returns to full. The turn comes through learning — back to the books and discipline that wake you from drift. Then accept the guide; the road to Tiantai is walked with a teacher, not alone. Snow melts; paths open.", aspects: ["Mist clears slow", "Study, then rise", "Round again", "Thawing recovery"] },
    { no: 86, grade: "上签", titleZh: "商辂中三元", title: "Shang Lu Wins Three Firsts", poemZh: "春来花发映阳台\n万里车来进宝财\n若得禹门三级浪\n恰如平地一声雷", poem: "Spring comes, flowers open, bright on the sunlit terrace;\nFrom ten thousand miles the carts arrive, bearing treasure.\nMount the three-fold wave at Yu's Gate —\nIt is exactly thunder from a level plain.", meaning: "Shang Lu took first place in all three examinations — the rare triple crown. This sign is cumulative success arriving at once: spring flowers, treasure carts from afar, the third wave over the Dragon Gate, and the thunderclap no one expected from flat ground. Long preparation converts to sudden renown. Accept the spotlight, keep an examinee's humility, and let the harvest be total.", aspects: ["Triple blessing", "Triple firsts", "Carts of treasure", "Thunder-strong health"] },
    { no: 87, grade: "中签", titleZh: "咬金探地穴", title: "Yaojin Explores the Underground Cave", poemZh: "人行半岭日衔山\n竣岭崖岩未可安\n仰望上天为护佑\n此身犹在太平间", poem: "You walk the mid-slope as the sun bites the mountain;\nSteep ridges and sheer cliffs — not yet safe ground.\nLook up and pray to heaven for its guarding;\nThis body still stands in the room of peace.", meaning: "Cheng Yaojin was lowered into the underworld and came back with treasure and a task. Halfway up, sun sinking, cliff on either side: the passage is genuinely exposed. Yet the sign's secret is the gaze — upward, not down at the drop. Protection is real and active; 'still in the room of peace' is a fact, not a hope. Keep praying, keep walking; the slope tops out ahead.", aspects: ["Prayed-for bond", "Exposed, guarded", "Steady, not rushed", "Held in peace"] },
    { no: 88, grade: "中签", titleZh: "庞洪畏包公", title: "Pang Hong Fears Judge Bao", poemZh: "林为一虎在当门\n须是有威不害人\n分明说是无防事\n忧恼迟疑恐惊心", poem: "In the wood there is a tiger standing at the gate;\nIt has the majesty, yet does no man harm.\nClearly said: there is nothing to guard against —\nBut worry, delay, and doubt alarm the heart.", meaning: "Pang Hong's fear of Judge Bao outlived the danger. The tiger at your gate has teeth but no intention: an authority or rule that looks like menace and is simply power. Nothing in the situation is actually coming for you — the harm is your own hesitation, the imagined pouncing. Verify once, face it once, then walk past. Courage here is not confrontation; it is refusing to rehearse the mauling.", aspects: ["Safe to pass", "Majesty, no harm", "Clear of danger", "Calm the nights"] },
    { no: 89, grade: "上签", titleZh: "大看琼花", title: "Viewing the Jade Flower", poemZh: "出入营谋大吉昌\n似玉无瑕石里藏\n若得贵人来指引\n斯时得宝喜风光", poem: "In every plan you move, great fortune and prosperity;\nLike flawless jade, hidden in the stone.\nShould a noble one come to point the way,\nThen the treasure is yours — joy and glory together.", meaning: "Emperor Yang journeyed to Yangzhou to behold the rare jade flower in bloom — the treasure rewards the pilgrimage. The flawless jade is currently encased in stone: your opportunity is real, yet not in plain sight. Do not chip at the stone from outside — find the guide whose word opens the gate, and the whole gem is yours. Ventures this season prosper. The gem will be unblemished; the pride public.", aspects: ["Flawless match", "Guided to the gem", "Unblemished gains", "Glory and glow"] },
    { no: 90, grade: "上签", titleZh: "苇佩遇仙", title: "Weipei Meets the Immortals", poemZh: "忽言一信向天飞\n泰山宝贝满船归\n若问路途成好事\n前头仍有贵人推", poem: "Suddenly word comes: a letter flies toward heaven;\nMount Tai's treasures return, a full shipload.\nAsk of the journey — good comes of the road;\nAhead there are still nobles to push you on.", meaning: "A reed-wearing wanderer met the immortals and returned laden. The news you half-dismissed is real — and flying: an acceptance, a summons, a remittance from Mount Tai. The return cargo is full — this journey, unlike others, pays. And the road does not end at the reward: another benefactor waits ahead, ready to push. Trust the good news, take the trip, thank the second door when it opens.", aspects: ["Flying letter, yes", "Rewarding road", "Full ship returns", "Lifted, refreshed"] },
    { no: 91, grade: "中签", titleZh: "三战吕布", title: "Three Duels with Lü Bu", poemZh: "好展愁眉出众来\n前途改变喜多财\n一条大路如天阔\n凡有施财尽畅怀", poem: "Now you may unfurrow that worried brow and come forth;\nThe road ahead changes — joy, and wealth beside.\nOne great highway, wide as the open sky;\nWhatever you lay out and spend, do so with an open heart.", meaning: "Three brothers together could match Lü Bu — numbers and unity turning stalemate into advance. The knotted phase is over: the road changes character ahead, and it is wide as the sky. Money flows both ways now — earnings rise, and generous spending is part of the sign, not a danger to it. Unclench the budget, unclench the brow, and move down the broad road with companions.", aspects: ["Broad road union", "Road opens wide", "Spend and gain", "Open-hearted health"] },
    { no: 92, grade: "上签", titleZh: "蔡卿报恩", title: "Cai Qing Repays a Kindness", poemZh: "自幼为商任设谋\n财禄盈丰不用求\n若是双身谋望事\n秀才出去状元回", poem: "From youth a merchant, free to lay his plans;\nWealth and salary brim full — no need to seek.\nIf two together plan what they would win,\nThe scholar goes out, and a laureate returns.", meaning: "Cai Qing repaid the kindness that lifted him, and the fortune doubled. Long-husbanded plans are maturing: prosperity arrives without being chased, because the groundwork was laid years back. Where two — partners, spouses, allies — move on a single plan, the result outranks the premise: set out a scholar, come home a top graduate. Gratitude is part of the mechanics: thank the one who opened the first door.", aspects: ["Doubled, together", "Outranks the plan", "Comes unbidden", "Brimming wellness"] },
    { no: 93, grade: "中签", titleZh: "高君保招亲", title: "Gao Junbao Wins a Bride", poemZh: "鸾凤翔毛雨淋漓\n当时却被雀儿欺\n终教一日云开达\n依旧还君整羽衣", poem: "The luan and phoenix beat through drenching rain,\nAnd for a time the sparrows mock and bully them;\nYet teach it so: one day the clouds open clear —\nAnd once more you are given back your sleek, groomed plumes.", meaning: "Gao Junbao was captured at the marriage-gate and won the bride anyway. Your feathered splendor is rain-soaked now, and smaller birds are bold against you — humiliation that is weather, not verdict. The promise is calendrical: clouds part on a set day, and the plumage returns groomed. Until then, do not peck back at sparrows; preen privately, keep the appointment, and let the sky clear. The match holds.", aspects: ["Soaked, then crowned", "Clears on schedule", "Preens back bright", "Dries and mends"] },
    { no: 94, grade: "下签", titleZh: "伯牙访友", title: "Boya Visits His Friend", poemZh: "君子莫体小人为\n事若差池惹是非\n琴鸣须用知音听\n守常安静得依稀", poem: "Let not the gentleman act as the small man acts;\nSlip but a little, and disputes are stirred.\nThe sounding qin must find a knowing ear;\nKeep to the quiet of the ordinary, and faintly it is had.", meaning: "Boya played for Ziqi because one friend truly heard. The warning is company: borrowing the small man's methods invites the disputes he lives on. Deeper: your music, work, or feeling needs the listener who understands it; playing to the wrong audience exhausts both sides. This is a season for the ordinary routine kept quietly, the knowing few over the crowd. The right ear will announce itself.", aspects: ["Await your hearer", "Mind your company", "Quiet, ordinary gains", "Quiet restores"] },
    { no: 95, grade: "中签", titleZh: "曹丕称帝", title: "Cao Pi Declares Himself Emperor", poemZh: "志气功业在朝朝\n今将酒色不胜饶\n若见金鸡报君语\n钱财福禄与君招", poem: "Ambition and achievement live in the daily mornings;\nBut now wine and pleasure are taken past restraint.\nShould the golden cock crow out its word to you,\nThen money, fortune, and favor come beckoning back.", meaning: "Cao Pi took the throne and then let indulgence eat the mornings. The ledger of this sign is precise: whatever you have built rests on dailiness, the morning discipline; the threat is not bad luck but intemperance, wine and ease one round too far. The golden cock is the alarm: heed the first honest warning, and money and favor return as before. The plot is recoverable.", aspects: ["Heed the alarm", "Keep mornings", "Returns on warning", "Temperance cures"] },
    { no: 96, grade: "上签", titleZh: "窦燕山积善", title: "Dou Yanshan Stores Up Goodness", poemZh: "巍峨宝塔不寻常\n八面玲珑尽放光\n劝君立志勤顶礼\n作善苍天降福祥", poem: "The towering pagoda is nothing common;\nEight-faced, exquisite, it shines on every side.\nI urge you: set your will, and bow with diligence;\nDo good, and grey heaven sends down blessing and fortune.", meaning: "Dou Yanshan, childless at thirty, reformed his life, did good quietly for years, and raised five brilliant sons. The pagoda is character built story by story — visible from eight directions because it is real. Your part is stated plainly: resolve, plus the daily bow, plus good deeds done without fanfare. Heaven's response is a deposit returned with interest. Start laying courses; light comes later and lasts.", aspects: ["Five sons blessed", "Tower of light", "Deposit plus interest", "Blessed health"] },
    { no: 97, grade: "中签", titleZh: "六出祁山", title: "Six Campaigns from Qishan", poemZh: "当风点烛空疏影\n恍惚铺成镜里花\n累被儿童求收拾\n怎知只是幻浮槎", poem: "A candle lit against the wind casts a thin, hollow shadow;\nWavering, it spreads into flowers in the mirror.\nAgain and again the children beg you to tidy it away —\nHow could they know it is only a drifting mirage-raft?", meaning: "Kongming marched six times from Qishan and six times returned — heroic effort against an unwinnable map. Look squarely at the chase: wind-candle light and mirror flowers — the prize has been an image all along. The children begging you to tidy up are the plain voices around you; they see it. Courage in this sign means auditing the campaign, not mounting a seventh. Withdraw honorably.", aspects: ["Mirage, pause", "Audit the campaign", "Mirror flowers only", "Rest from marches"] },
    { no: 98, grade: "下签", titleZh: "吉平遇难", title: "Ji Ping Meets Misfortune", poemZh: "出入求谋事宜迟\n只恐闲愁惹是非\n如鸟飞入罗网内\n脱困能有几多时", poem: "In going out and in, in every scheme — the time is late;\nMost of all, idle sorrow stirs up harm.\nLike a bird flown into the net,\nHow much time remains to struggle free?", meaning: "Ji Ping, the loyal physician, was betrayed mid-plot and executed. The scheme you are carrying is late, exposed, and inside the net; watchers hold every string. Idle worry, the poem adds, is itself an offense — it leaks. This is the hour for silence, not escape plans: consult almost no one, postpone everything postponable, and let attention pass. Fluttering birds tighten the net; still birds outlast the hunter.", aspects: ["Silence now", "Postpone all", "Netted, be still", "Stillness preserves"] },
    { no: 99, grade: "下签", titleZh: "陶三春挂帅", title: "Tao Sanchun Takes Command", poemZh: "勒马持鞭直过来\n半有忧危半有灾\n恰似遭火焚烧屋\n天降时雨荡成灰", poem: "Reining the horse, whip in hand, you charge straight on;\nHalf the way is peril, half the way is harm.\nJust so a house caught in burning fire —\nHeaven sends a timely rain, and all is washed to ash.", meaning: "Tao Sanchun, the woman marshal, rode into campaigns that burned everything. Your charge carries peril on both halves of the road, and the house is already burning: even the rescuing rain finds only ashes. Dismount; do not marshal more force. Save what can be saved — people, health, reputation — and exit the burning structure. Rain will fall; ground washed to ash grows again.", aspects: ["Exit the fire", "Dismount now", "Ash, then rebuild", "Escape the smoke"] },
    { no: 100, grade: "下签", titleZh: "三教谈道", title: "Three Teachings Discuss the Dao", poemZh: "佛神灵通与君知\n痴人说事转昏迷\n老人求得灵签去\n不如守旧待时来", poem: "Buddha and the spirits, with their insight, let you know:\nA fool telling over his affairs turns only more confused.\nThe old man draws his sacred lot and goes his way —\nBetter keep the old, and wait for the time to come.", meaning: "The three sages agreed on the oldest rule: fools theorize themselves dizzy. You keep retelling your situation, seeking the reading that fits the wish; each retelling adds fog. The oracle's answer to the old man was not another plan but a posture: keep the old way, keep the old store, and wait for the season. Close the debate; let time think. Clarity returns when chatter stops.", aspects: ["Stop retelling", "Keep the old", "Hold, don't chase", "Quiet restores"] }
  ],
};
